---
import Reference from '../layouts/Reference.astro';
import CompetencyExamples from '../components/CompetencyExamples.astro';
import {
  SHARED_COMPETENCIES,
  COMPETENCY_EXAMPLE_THEMES,
} from '../data/shared-competencies';
---

<Reference
  title="Shared skills for working with AI"
  description="Choose a skill and your role for practical guidance, everyday AI-assisted work examples and a small exercise to help you improve."
>
  <h1>Shared skills for working with AI</h1>
  <p class="skill-intro">
    Good AI-assisted work takes more than a useful tool. HELM suggests five
    competencies—skills and behaviors you can practice—to help you make good
    choices, work with others and take responsibility for results.
  </p>
  <p>
    Choose a skill you want to develop, then your role. Each guide gives you
    practical steps, an example and a small exercise. These ideas build on{' '}
    <a href="/foundation">HELM’s six principles</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="five-shared-skills">Five skills to practice</h2>
  <ol class="skill-definitions" role="list">
    {SHARED_COMPETENCIES.map((competency, index) => (
      <li>
        <h3 id={competency.id}>
          <span aria-hidden="true">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          {competency.title}
        </h3>
        <div class="skill-definition-copy">
          <p>{competency.description}</p>
          <a
            class="skill-practice-link"
            href={`#${COMPETENCY_EXAMPLE_THEMES[0].id}-${competency.id}`}
            data-practice-target="competency-examples"
            data-practice-competency={competency.id}
          >
            Practice {competency.title}
          </a>
        </div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h2 id="examples">Build a skill in your role</h2>
  <p>
    Pick one competency to work on. The expectations stay the same across roles;
    the guidance helps you put them into practice in your own work. The examples
    are illustrative situations to learn from and adapt.
  </p>
  <CompetencyExamples />

  <h2 id="try-it">Choose one thing to practice</h2>
  <p>Pick a recent piece of AI-assisted work and discuss:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Which of these behaviors helped, or would have helped?</li>
    <li>What example from the work supports that view?</li>
    <li>What will you practice on the next similar task?</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Consider the opportunity and support people had. If there is not enough
    evidence, say so. Use this for learning and feedback; a formal evaluation
    method is still being developed.
  </p>
</Reference>

<style>
  .skill-intro {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }

  .skill-definitions {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .skill-definitions li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    break-inside: avoid;
  }

  .skill-definitions h3 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .skill-definitions h3 span {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .skill-definitions p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-ink-light);
  }

  .skill-practice-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    .skill-definitions li {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
